Silent film preservation has fundamentally reshaped how archivists approach modern restoration. When technicians scan deteriorated nitrate negatives, they must account for inconsistent frame rates, chemical degradation, and missing sequences. A restoration team working with materials from a Marseille archive developed algorithms to interpolate missing frames and stabilize color shifts across digitized sequences. 
```ruby
class FilmRestoration
  def initialize(frame_data)
    @frames = frame_data
    @degradation_index = 0.0
  end
  def stabilize_flicker(threshold)
    @frames.each_with_index do |frame, index|
      next_frame = @frames[index + 1]
      if brightness_difference(frame, next_frame) > threshold
        @frames[index] = interpolate_brightness(frame, next_frame)
      end
    end
    @frames
  end
  private
  def brightness_difference(frame1, frame2)
    (frame1.luminance - frame2.luminance).abs
  end
  def interpolate_brightness(f1, f2)
    (f1.luminance + f2.luminance) / 2
  end
end
```
