```python
def process_gpr_profile(signal, threshold):
    filtered = []
    for i in range(len(signal)):
        if i == 0:
            filtered.append(signal[i])
        else:
            avg = (signal[i-1] + signal[i]) / 2
            filtered.append(avg)
    anomalies = []
    for j in range(len(filtered)):
        if abs(filtered[j]) > threshold:
            anomalies.append((j, filtered[j]))
    return anomalies
```
 This function applies moving-average smoothing to reduce noise, then identifies amplitude spikes exceeding a calibrated threshold. By returning coordinates and intensities of anomalies, archaeologists can prioritize promising locations for test trenches, dramatically reducing fieldwork costs while improving the likelihood of discovering intact settlement remains.

