```php
function detectAnomalies($gprData, $threshold) {
    $anomalies = array();
    $baseline = array_sum($gprData) / count($gprData);
    foreach ($gprData as $depth => $amplitude) {
        $deviation = abs($amplitude - $baseline);
        if ($deviation > $threshold) {
            $anomalies[] = array(
                'depth' => $depth,
                'amplitude' => $amplitude,
                'deviation' => $deviation
            );
        }
    }
    return $anomalies;
}
```
 This approach filters noise and highlights significant reflections corresponding to buried walls, hearths, or refuse pits. When properly calibrated with soil conductivity measurements, GPR surveys can reveal settlement patterns spanning multiple centuries, fundamentally transforming our understanding of prehistoric occupation.

